# Saving the pane and tab arrangement and reopening it — the whole session round trip against the
# real shell. `session` captures what closing the window would save, prunes it the way a launch
# does, and rebuilds it in place, so the assertions after it are about what actually came back.

tree .
refresh

# An arrangement worth losing: two panes, and three tabs in the first.
newtab Documents
newtab Pictures
assert-tabs 3
split right Documents
assert-panes 2

session

# Everything survived the round trip.
assert-panes 2
assert-tabs 1

# The pane that was active is the one still active, and it is showing the folder it was showing.
assert-path Documents

# Back to the first pane (panes are 1-indexed here): its three tabs came back too.
pane 1
assert-tabs 3

assert-not-launched
state

# Ctrl+Shift+T: the pane remembers what it closed.
newtab Documents
assert-tabs 4
closetab
assert-tabs 3
reopen
assert-tabs 4
assert-path Documents
